---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const d='/equipment/15-10/',brochure='https://premedpharma.hu/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Envisu_C2300_EBrochure_2017_enpph.pdf',archive='https://www.leica-microsystems.com/products/surgical-microscopes/p/envisu-c2300/';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Envisu C2300 inactive cart and independent graphic card" description="Orbit an inactive Bioptigen/Leica Envisu C2300 and inspect missing or paired marks on a separate graphic card." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment" id="envisu"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/15-10/">← Equipment 15-10</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#en-evidence">References and checks</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">15-10 / INACTIVE EXTERIOR · DETACHED ART CARD</p><h2>A missing mark is not a distance of zero</h2><p class="eq-lede">Inspect the closed Envisu C2300 cart and opaque display head. The separate, fixed classroom graphic demonstrates the difference between a pair of marks and missing data.</p></header>
<div class="en-cols"><section><h3>Sealed cart and fixed display shell</h3><canvas id="en-model" aria-label="Orbitable Envisu C2300 cart with blank monitor, sealed hand head and unrelated art stand"></canvas><p id="en-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="en-front">Reset overview</button><button id="en-case">Cart and head close-up</button><button id="en-board">Detached art board</button></section>
<section><h3>Fixed 2D graphic</h3><label>Independent column<select id="en-column"><option value="0">A · paired marks</option><option value="3">D · missing lower mark</option><option value="5">F · paired marks</option></select></label><button id="en-next">Next illustrated column</button>
<svg id="en-diagram" viewBox="0 0 92 67" role="img" aria-label="Authored light rectangular marks in columns, one missing mark">
<defs><pattern id="en-lattice" width="13" height="5" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x="6"><path d="M13 0H0V5" fill="none" stroke="#395c66" stroke-width=".28"/></pattern></defs><rect width="92" height="67" fill="#20343a"/><rect width="92" height="67" fill="url(#en-lattice)"/><rect id="en-highlight" y="9" width="10" height="47" fill="#d5a35a" fill-opacity=".23" stroke="#d5a35a" stroke-width=".45"/><g id="en-art"/><line id="en-gap" y1="24.5" y2="49.5" stroke="#ffc981" stroke-width=".55" stroke-dasharray="2 1"/>
<g fill="#c3dbd7" font-size="3.7" font-family="system-ui" text-anchor="middle"><text x="13" y="61">A</text><text x="26" y="61">B</text><text x="39" y="61">C</text><text x="52" y="61">D</text><text x="65" y="61">E</text><text x="78" y="61">F</text></g></svg>
<p id="en-readout" role="status"></p><p>Each row step is 4 fictional graphic units. One missing mark leaves the value unknown. The same artwork is used for every selection; it is not a scanner output.</p><button id="en-export">Download graphic summary</button><p><a href={d+'example-art.json'}>Example paired result</a>.</p></section></div>
<section id="en-evidence"><h3>Selected case and checks</h3><div class="en-cols">
<figure><img src={d+'station.webp'} alt="Original Envisu C2300 closed cart, blank screen and separate graphic stand"/><figcaption>Original overall view. The <a href={brochure+'#page=1'}>Leica 2017 brochure cover photograph</a> informs its casters, tall monitor, open shelf structure and visible closed housings; <a href={archive}>Leica’s archived product page</a> identifies the C2300 family. This scene has no cables, connections, controls or simulated movement.</figcaption></figure>
<figure><img src={d+'case.webp'} alt="Original closer render of the sealed white head model on the static cart top"/><figcaption>Original close-up. <a href={brochure+'#page=2'}>Leica manufacturer side photo of the detached head</a> establishes the white body and dark nose shape. The model closes the nose with an opaque blank and omits optical components; the rest and component details are inferred.</figcaption></figure></div>
<table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual / source</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Cart with monitor W × H × D</td><td>787 × 1,549 × 559 mm</td><td><a href={brochure+'#page=9'}>Brochure p. 9, physical features</a>; approximate exterior checked within 2 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Sealed head W × H × D</td><td>80 × 170 × 230 mm</td><td>Same physical features table; external approximation only</td></tr><tr><td>Paired marks</td><td>5 rows × 4 = 20 graphic units</td><td>Exact</td></tr><tr><td>Missing mark</td><td>Unknown, not zero</td><td>Returned as null</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>The detached drawing calculates vertical spacing only if both fixed marks are present. No optical operation, positioning, acquisition, clinical workflow, treatment, specimen or tissue is represented. The register’s original application test is unsupported.</p><p><a href={d+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={d+'envisu-c2300.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={d+'art.mjs'}>Fixed graphic and report logic</a> · <a href={d+'vr.json'}>VR target bounds</a>. Headset use not verified.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/15-10/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>
#envisu .en-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.15fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#envisu section{margin:1rem 0;padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);min-width:0}
#envisu :is(button,select){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.4rem;margin:.2rem .25rem .2rem 0;max-width:100%}#envisu button{cursor:pointer}#envisu :is(button,select):focus-visible{outline:2px solid #b28d5e}
#en-model{width:100%;height:354px;display:block;touch-action:none}#en-diagram{width:min(100%,340px);display:block;margin:.45rem auto}#envisu figure{margin:.5rem 0}#envisu figure img{width:100%}
#envisu table{width:100%;font-size:.94rem;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left}#envisu td,#envisu th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem}
@media(max-width:850px){#envisu .en-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#en-model{height:282px}}
</style>
